{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/601701-vampire-organization-in-new-york-city-questions","id":601701,"title":"Vampire Organization in New York City Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-24T06:27:35-07:00","id":601701,"title":"Vampire Organization in New York City Questions","content":"Hello I'm running a demon game currently and some plays wanted to cause some problems with vampires and this got me thinking. How would vampires e Organized in New York City.<br /> <br /> Each Borough alone is as large as a city. Do you think that Each Borough would have it own prince ?<br /> <br /> I mean when you look at it there are 5 clans and 5 Borough it seems like a perfect fit.<br /> <br /> Anyway I'm looking for some advice from players with alot more information.<br /> <br /> Also how would a powerful vampire handle some one murdering there most cherished ghoul ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T08:42:13-07:00","id":601871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/601701-vampire-organization-in-new-york-city-questions#post601701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each Borough alone is as large as a city. Do you think that Each Borough would have it own prince ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. At the very least each borough could be the domain of a powerful elder or faction. It might be more interesting (but also more work) to have the Kindred society of the city brake down on lines which don't quite match the human political divisions, with differing organizations controlling chunks of multiple boroughs, but rarely controlling an entire borough. NYC is so big and so densely populated that a huge number of vampires could reside there, too many for one covenant to easily govern. I suspect that's why it was depicted as a war zone in V:tM. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/601701-vampire-organization-in-new-york-city-questions#post601701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean when you look at it there are 5 clans and 5 Borough it seems like a perfect fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>And 5 Covenants, which adds an extra possibilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/601701-vampire-organization-in-new-york-city-questions#post601701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how would a powerful vampire handle some one murdering there most cherished ghoul ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the specific circumstances, but generally speaking it would be considered a direct personal attack and dealt with violently.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T11:25:09-07:00","id":602034,"title":"","content":"One option for cities as big and contested as New York is to have a ruling council rather than a single Prince. Of course, this situation only remains stable until the game starts...<br /> <br /> Since &quot;vampires in a huge city with lots of pseudo-Gothic skyscrapers and a long history of crime and weirdness&quot; is such a classic setup, I'd be tempted to do something weird with it to run counter to expectations.<br /> <br /> For example, the player characters discover that no vampires reside in Manhattan. Why not?<br /> <br /> For a less extreme example, the city might just have seen a coup by one covenant, so there are lots of gaps in the political small-i infrastructure where a vampire would normally have influence.<br /> <br /> As for the ghoul issue, as Vyrkolash says it depends on the vampire and other circumstances, but it probably won't be very nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T11:36:14-07:00","id":602043,"title":"","content":"It seems like one of the players wants to sneak into vampire society and destroy it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T11:36:23-07:00","id":602044,"title":"","content":"In my version of New York I had a High Prince who pulled a corporate type takeover who oversees a council of lords, different sections of the city in effect still have their own prince who would dearly love to overthrow the High Prince. The end result is a set of common laws that are routinely ignored when you can get away with it, while the individual lords just have to exercise a little more discretion to run their own fiefs as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T12:10:30-07:00","id":602066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/601701-vampire-organization-in-new-york-city-questions?p=602043#post602043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like one of the players wants to sneak into vampire society and destroy it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, since it's a Demon game, you could put him up against the Holy Engineers from The Danse Macabre. The God Machine sends them messages from the future, so he'd be up against Vampires who know he's coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T22:42:11-07:00","id":603513,"title":"","content":"As some one has set my Chronicle's in the Rotten Apple before that became a term in the OWoD. I'll offer some help in the Vampire side of things because out of my three games VtR was the most fleshed out part a part of New York City.<br /> <br /> In my version of things the Lancea et Sanctum took over NYC from the Invictus centuries ago, They enforced their vision harshly, letting the other Covenants exists, but only if they accepted the idea that the Sanctum ruled first. Then in the mid 90s the Carthians and the Invictius with help of the Ordo Dracul took back NYC.... that's when things got interesting.<br /> <br /> A Nosferatu &quot;Prince Pro Tempera&quot; of the the Invictus abdicated his throne and every Clan and Covenant tried to claim Princehood. In the end an 250 year old Unbound took over and divided the 5 Boroughs into separate Domains. Keeping Manhattan for herself and dividing the others by the other Covenants except for the Lancea et Sanctum. She declared herself &quot;Duchess&quot; and the other borough head's her &quot;<span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Marquess.&quot; </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She had a set of 25 hounds called her &quot;Paper Dolls&quot; who she would dress, make up, and send out to make sure she maintained control. She was based on one of the Damnation City Princes but became her own character. Let me know if you want to know more.<br /> <br /> Last thing I'll say is that in my chronicle their were 300+ vampires in NYC.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T01:43:30-07:00","id":603649,"title":"","content":"I'd like to hear more. I know about the Paper Dolls Prince, that's from the Tyrant, I used her myself with some changes, very fun character. She sort of begs to be overthrown, but her erratic behavior is too dangerously unpredictable, potentially turning rivals into allies and allies into mulch, making it a really risky idea. Plus as a potentially more tragic character you can have a lot of fun developing her background. At least, played by the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T04:38:50-07:00","id":914003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/601701-vampire-organization-in-new-york-city-questions?p=603513#post603513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As some one has set my Chronicle's in the Rotten Apple before that became a term in the OWoD. I'll offer some help in the Vampire side of things because out of my three games VtR was the most fleshed out part a part of New York City.<br /> <br /> In my version of things the Lancea et Sanctum took over NYC from the Invictus centuries ago, They enforced their vision harshly, letting the other Covenants exists, but only if they accepted the idea that the Sanctum ruled first. Then in the mid 90s the Carthians and the Invictius with help of the Ordo Dracul took back NYC.... that's when things got interesting.<br /> <br /> A Nosferatu &quot;Prince Pro Tempera&quot; of the the Invictus abdicated his throne and every Clan and Covenant tried to claim Princehood. In the end an 250 year old Unbound took over and divided the 5 Boroughs into separate Domains. Keeping Manhattan for herself and dividing the others by the other Covenants except for the Lancea et Sanctum. She declared herself &quot;Duchess&quot; and the other borough head's her &quot;<span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Marquess.&quot; </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She had a set of 25 hounds called her &quot;Paper Dolls&quot; who she would dress, make up, and send out to make sure she maintained control. She was based on one of the Damnation City Princes but became her own character. Let me know if you want to know more.<br /> <br /> Last thing I'll say is that in my chronicle their were 300+ vampires in NYC.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yea I figured for every 100 or so humans there is 1 vampire so in my game. So that makes for a 1000+<br /> <br /> I have all the lines in my game. Its a continuous world were everyone's games can affect each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T06:05:50-07:00","id":914039,"title":"","content":"My recommendation would be to not worry about the scope of the city so much as the story you are wanting to tell. One thousand vampires is a large number, and while the city could theoretically support them, it would be daunting as a GM to even come up with concepts for one hundred. You mentioned that it was a Demon game, perhaps the Fallen only know of one &quot;faction&quot; of vampires, encamped in one of the boroughs, who have a Prince, court, and the like. While infiltrating, they find out that the other boroughs are forbidden to the Kindred of their current borough, and very little is known of what happens in the others. Gives you a mystery angle to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11942-the13thghost","name":"The13thGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T20:18:35-07:00","id":922398,"title":"","content":"In the Joe Pitt Casebooks, which are recommended in the 2e core, most of the action is centered around Manhattan, which all of the vampires see as an island of civilization in a sea of insanity. Within Manhattan, there are four major factions, two of which map fairly well to the Invictus and the Carthians- one is basically equal parts Wall Street firm and mob, the other is a revolutionary group whose members were all part of a political, social, or sexual minority in life. The other two are a bit less one-to-one: one comes off like an unholy combination of the Ordo Dracul and the Circle of the Crone, while the other is basically a vampiric gang that owns Harlem. The outer boroughs don't get a whole lot of focus, and are kind of considered no-man's land, but the groups that operate in them are similar to the Circle of the Crone in feel. There are some smaller factions in Manhattan, which basically map to minor covenants or independent coteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}